faces point demand toward lower-intensity energy in the 18-36 month run-up to 2030: the regulations rows fix FuelEU limits 6% below the 2020 reference from 2030 and 14,5% from 2035 for ships under the Regulation [item_forward_events:cfb6faf5-67ff-4b0e-8f60-80f07a7b3d5a], and the market-surface analysis calls the IMO strategy's aim of 5-10% zero or near-zero GHG energy in 2030 a strong demand signal to fuel suppliers [section_claim_provenance:3312903a-3657-41c1-9fe4-1d037b592a7d]. The two differ in baseline, metric and scope and are not added together.",
